9fdb-6d64ec4e0ac2","uri":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/1632941531","locality":"Wildflower Garden, Black Hill Conservation Park. This koala came up Addison Ave, and entered the park. It sat in the shade near the building, and accepted several drinks of water.","notes":"The koala came up Addison Ave, outside the park, along the footpath, and game in through the gate.  I headed along the path towards a shady area near the building. It stopped when it noticed me, and watched me for a while.  It checked a couple of trees (planted melaleucas) and I thought it had climbed one, but shortly after, I noticed it had returned to the ground, and was lying spread out somewhat on a rock on the ground.  I offered it water and it drank.  Returning the next day, it was still in the same location. I offered it water again, and it drank. An hour later I offered more water and it drank again.  Each time, I offered it only a small amount of water from a running hose, leaving it run for maybe 2 minutes as it lapped it up. The third day the weather was cooler over night, and it was no-where to be seen, a small pile of droppings (they were not remarkable) were left, near where it had been. It was a mature male, with the gland markings on the chest. It appeared to be in good condition, apart from its unusual behaviour.","recordStatus":"Confident","photos":[{"url":"https://images.ala.org.au/image/proxyImageThumbnailLarge?imageId=4460b3ed-8b1a-45cf-a4ef-354397a77113","license":"CC BY","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","creator":"John Fleming"}]}],["1632959304",138.73197,-34.89603,17132,20,2,1,50,"",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"2016-11-27T09:45",{"version":1,"datasetKey":"84a649ce-ff81-420d-9c41-aa1de59e3766","occurrenceId":"a7efe428-d0f9-44a6-a662-1c353efc0525","uri":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/1632959304","locality":"13 Smiths Gully Rd, Montacute SA 5134, Australia","recordStatus":"confident","photos":[{"url":"https://images.ala.org.au/i